{"tag":"section","attrib":{"id":"id5d11523a-86b3-11f1-aae1-ab9d2cf5dce1","identifier":"/us/usc/t12/s281"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"281"},"text":"§ 281.","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Capital","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"No Federal reserve bank shall commence business with a subscribed capital less than $4,000,000.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":null},{"tag":"sourceCredit","attrib":{"id":"id5d11523b-86b3-11f1-aae1-ab9d2cf5dce1"},"text":"(","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1913-12-23/ch6/s2"},"text":"Dec. 23, 1913, ch. 6, § 2","children":[],"tail":" (part), "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/38/253"},"text":"38 Stat. 253","children":[],"tail":".)"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"notes","attrib":{"type":"uscNote","id":"id5d11523c-86b3-11f1-aae1-ab9d2cf5dce1"},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"note","attrib":{"role":"crossHeading","topic":"editorialNotes","id":"id5d11523d-86b3-11f1-aae1-ab9d2cf5dce1"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"b","attrib":{},"text":"Editorial Notes","children":[],"tail":null}],"tail":null}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"codification","id":"id5d11523e-86b3-11f1-aae1-ab9d2cf5dce1"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Codification","children":[],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Section is comprised of part of the thirteenth par. of section 2 of act ","children":[{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1913-12-23"},"text":"Dec. 23, 1913","children":[],"tail":". Some of the other provisions of the thirteenth par. are classified to "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t12/s224"},"text":"section 224 of this title","children":[],"tail":", and some were not included in the Code. For classification of other pars. of section 2 of this Act, see Codification note set out under "},{"tag":"ref","